---

Why this file exists, and what to consider changing

A public repository with no licence file is not "open" — it is *all rights
reserved by default*, and nobody may legally copy or reuse it. That default
is the right one for software you intend to sell, but leaving it implicit
means nobody can tell what they are allowed to do, and some hosts and stores
ask for an explicit licence. This file states the default rather than
changing it.

If you would rather the project were open source, that is a deliberate and
**effectively irreversible** decision: a permissive licence, once published,
cannot be recalled from the copies people already have. Decide it on purpose,
not by leaving the field blank.
